 "title": "Head and neck infection decision chart: a sore throat is pharyngitis unless the signs show spread (peritonsillar abscess with uvula deviation, deep neck space infection with trismus and reduced neck movement); a toxic patient a week after pharyngitis suggests Lemierre syndrome and a diabetic or immunocompromised patient with a necrotic palate suggests mucormycosis; each column gives clues, workup and treatment",
